# Tutorial 16 — Testing and Release
# Validation, playtesting, save/load testing, the release checklist, and post-release.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_16_testing_release
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}
{{BG_DECL}}@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
{{BG_START}}
[textspeed 28]
[autodelay 1650]
[show lavender center happy]
[wait 200]
Lavender: This is the last tutorial. Everything you've learned only matters if the game ships and works.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Testing, validation, and the release checklist. Let's finish strong.

@label lesson_menu
[show lavender far_left talking]
> Editor validation — automated checks -> section_validation
> Playtesting — systematic manual testing -> section_playtesting
> Save/load testing — the subtle bugs -> section_saves
> The release checklist -> section_release
> Post-release — what happens after you ship -> section_post_release
> Quick reference: release gate -> quick_reference
> Final quiz -> practice_scene
> Back to Tutorial Hub -> return_hub

# ─── Quick Reference ─────────────────────────────────────────────

@label quick_reference
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Do not ship from vibes. Ship from a checklist:
narrator: {b}Validate{/b}: parser, assets, labels, menu config.
narrator: {b}Playtest{/b}: every branch, every ending, every tutorial or route entry.
narrator: {b}Save/load{/b}: before choices, after branches, inside subroutines, near scene exits.
narrator: {b}Package{/b}: clean build, fresh install, launch from shortcut, verify logs.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Checklist: one final pass on a clean machine or clean folder before you call the build done.
> Start the lesson sections -> section_validation
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Validation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_validation
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: The editor catches structural errors before you play. Three automated checks:
narrator: {b}Parser validation{/b} — syntax errors, missing [endif], malformed commands, broken tag nesting.
narrator: {b}Asset validation{/b} — every @background, @charimg, [bgm], and [sfx] path points to a file that actually exists.
narrator: {b}Label graph{/b} — every [jump], [goto], and choice arrow {b}>{/b} target resolves to an existing @label.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Run validation before every playtest. It takes seconds. It catches hours of debugging.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: A clean validation pass means the script is {b}structurally sound{/b}. It doesn't mean the game is correct — logic bugs need human eyes.
> Next: playtesting -> section_playtesting
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Playtesting ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_playtesting
[show lavender right talking]
Lavender: No tool replaces playing your own game. Here's the systematic approach:
narrator: {b}1. Play every branch.{/b} Click every choice. Follow every path to its end. No shortcuts.
narrator: {b}2. Watch pacing.{/b} Does textspeed feel right? Are waits too long? Lines too short?
narrator: {b}3. Check staging.{/b} Is anyone on the wrong side? Do expressions match the dialogue?
narrator: {b}4. Listen.{/b} Does music loop cleanly? Are SFX timed correctly? Any silence gaps?
narrator: {b}5. Read the text.{/b} Spelling, grammar, punctuation. Read every line as if seeing it for the first time.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Keep a notepad open. Write down every issue, no matter how small. Fix in batches after the session.
Lavender: Then get someone else to play. Watch them — don't explain anything. Fresh eyes catch what you've gone blind to.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Test after each chapter, not only at the end. Small frequent tests beat one marathon debugging session.
> Next: save/load -> section_saves
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Save/Load Testing ──────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_saves
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Save/load is where the subtlest bugs live. Test each of these:
narrator: {b}Save mid-dialogue.{/b} Reload. Does text resume from the correct line?
narrator: {b}Save before a choice.{/b} Reload. Are the choice buttons still present?
narrator: {b}Save after a branch.{/b} Reload. Are variables correct? Does the story remember your path?
narrator: {b}Save inside a [call] block.{/b} Reload. Does [return] still work?
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: Edge cases:
narrator: {b}Save at the very first line of a file.{/b} Reload.
narrator: {b}Save at the last line of a scene.{/b} Reload.
narrator: {b}Overwrite an existing save.{/b} Load the overwritten slot. Does it load the new state?
narrator: {b}Save in one chapter, load in another.{/b} Does the engine restore the correct scene?
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: If save/load works at every scene transition and branch point, you're in good shape.
> Next: release checklist -> section_release
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Release Checklist ───────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_release
[show lavender right talking]
Lavender: Run this checklist before shipping. Every item must pass.
narrator: {b}☐ All branches tested.{/b} Every choice leads somewhere. No dead ends.
narrator: {b}☐ All assets present.{/b} No placeholder images, no missing audio files.
narrator: {b}☐ Variables verified.{/b} Counters and flags produce correct outcomes in every path.
narrator: {b}☐ Text proofread.{/b} Spelling, grammar, punctuation — every line.
narrator: {b}☐ UI tested at target resolution.{/b} Nothing overlaps, nothing is cut off.
[show lavender center talking]
narrator: {b}☐ Locale files complete{/b} (if localized). No raw key names visible in any language.
narrator: {b}☐ Save/load verified{/b} at every critical point.
narrator: {b}☐ Menu navigation works.{/b} Title, settings, save, load — all reachable and functional.
narrator: {b}☐ All endings reachable.{/b} Can the player actually finish the game from every route?
narrator: {b}☐ Audio levels balanced.{/b} No track is too loud or too quiet relative to others.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: If any item fails, you're not ready. Fix it, retest, then check the list again.
> Next: post-release -> section_post_release
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Post-Release ────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_post_release
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: You shipped. Congratulations. But it's not quite over:
narrator: {b}Monitor feedback.{/b} Players will find bugs you didn't. Respond quickly to critical ones.
narrator: {b}Keep a changelog.{/b} Document every fix and update. Players appreciate transparency.
narrator: {b}Don't panic-patch.{/b} Test your fixes before pushing them. A bad hotfix is worse than the original bug.
narrator: {b}Take a break.{/b} You earned it. Come back to feedback with fresh energy.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Every shipped game teaches you more than ten unfinished ones. Be proud of what you built.
> Final quiz -> practice_scene
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Final Quiz ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label practice_scene
[set final_score 0]
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Last tutorial, last quiz. Three questions about shipping discipline.

@label fq1
Lavender: Q1: A choice leads to a blank screen. Most likely cause?
> Missing @label for the target -> fq1_correct
> A typo in a variable name -> fq1_wrong
> Save file corruption -> fq1_wrong

@label fq1_correct
[inc final_score]
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Right. The choice arrow points to a label that doesn't exist or is misspelled.
[jump fq2]

@label fq1_wrong
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: This is a navigation error — the choice target has no matching @label. Variable typos and save bugs cause different symptoms.
[jump fq2]

@label fq2
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Q2: When should you start testing?
> After each major section -> fq2_correct
> After the game is completely finished -> fq2_wrong
> Testing is optional for small projects -> fq2_wrong

@label fq2_correct
[inc final_score]
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Exactly. Test as you go. Bugs caught early are cheap. Bugs caught at release are expensive.
[jump fq3]

@label fq2_wrong
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Waiting until the end piles up all bugs at once. Test each section as you finish it — no exceptions, no matter the project size.
[jump fq3]

@label fq3
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Q3: You find a critical bug 2 hours after release. What do you do?
> Push a fix immediately without testing -> fq3_wrong
> Test the fix, then push a patch -> fq3_correct
> Ignore it and hope nobody notices -> fq3_wrong

@label fq3_correct
[inc final_score]
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Right. Test before you push. A bad hotfix is worse than the original bug.
[jump final_result]

@label fq3_wrong
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Always test your fix first. Panic-patching often creates new bugs. And ignoring critical bugs destroys player trust.
[jump final_result]

@label final_result
[show lavender center talking]
[if final_score >= 3]
Lavender: 3/3. Shipping discipline is solid. You'll release with confidence.
[elif final_score == 2]
Lavender: 2/3. Almost there. Tighten the weak spot before it matters.
[elif final_score == 1]
Lavender: 1/3. Worth reviewing the checklist section before your first release.
[else]
Lavender: 0/3. Better to learn these here than in front of players. That's what tutorials are for.
[endif]
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: That's the full tour — from the first dialogue line to the last release checklist.
Lavender: Build something, test it honestly, and ship it. I'll be here when you need a second pass.
> Retake the quiz -> practice_scene
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_16]
[flag tutorial_done_16]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[goto {{HUB_TARGET}}:topics_page_3]
